  "previousGoalTurn": "Progress: C66 implementation, tests, cleanup and remote-exact checkpoint completed. C67 continues the full ecosystem and current NuGet objective.",
  "findings": [
    "Three native build/test jobs did not establish that the final managed/native NuGet packages ran on all advertised platforms; the old publisher packed and consumed only on Windows.",
    "Eleven directly or transitively invoked NuGet Bash scripts had Git mode 100644, although WSL on the Windows filesystem could execute them."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Build native libraries, pack/audit once, run isolated package consumers on win-x64/linux-x64/linux-arm64, then enter protected publication.",
    "Each consumer checks the actual Node platform/architecture before execution.",
    "Consumers and publisher download the same current-run package artifact; include its audit and hashes; do not repack after consumer validation.",
    "Only the final job requests the nuget-release environment, API-key secret or OIDC write permission.",
    "Build report validators in the final job because previous job build output is not shared.",
    "Set executable Git modes on eleven current Bash entry points without changing their blobs.",
    "Preserve mandatory publication readiness, exact public graph, feed-current and package-hash gates."
  ],
